## 4. Python Code — Explanation

### 4.1 [train_mumbai_model.py](file:///c:/Users/rajan/Downloads/JavaProject/python_scripts/train_mumbai_model.py) — Model Training

Yeh script **ek baar run karni hoti hai** — model train karne ke liye.

#### Step-by-step kya hota hai:

**Step 1 — Data Load karo:**
```python
df = pd.read_csv(csv_file)
```
CSV file padh ke pandas DataFrame mein load karo.

**Step 2 — Cleaning:**
```python
df.dropna(subset=number_cols + [target_col], inplace=True)
```
- Missing values wali rows hata do
- Outlier prices hata do (bahut saste ya bahut mehnge)
- Text columns mein missing = most common value se fill karo

**Step 3 — Feature Engineering:**
```python
df["room_ratio"]  = df["bedroom_num"] / (df["bathroom_num"] + 1)
df["total_rooms"] = df["bedroom_num"] + df["bathroom_num"] + df["balcony_num"]
```
Extra features banao jo model ko better predict karne mein help karte hain.

**Step 4 — Locality Cleanup:**
```python
top_localities = df["locality"].value_counts().nlargest(80).index.tolist()
df["locality"] = df["locality"].apply(lambda x: x if x in top_localities else "Other")
```
80 most common localities rakhte hain, baaki sab "Other" ho jaate hain.

**Step 5 — X aur y banao:**
```python
X = df[number_cols + text_cols]   # inputs
y = np.log1p(df[target_col])      # log of price
```
> `log1p` isliye use kiya kyunki prices bahut bade hote hain — log lene se model better seekhta hai.

**Step 6 — Encode + Scale:**
```python
encoder = OneHotEncoder(...)
X_train_cat = encoder.fit_transform(X_train[text_cols])   # text → numbers

scaler = StandardScaler()
X_train_num = scaler.fit_transform(X_train[number_cols])  # scale numbers
```
Text ko numbers mein convert karo (One-Hot Encoding).  
Numbers ko same scale pe laao (StandardScaler).

**Step 7 — Train:**
```python
model = GradientBoostingRegressor(n_estimators=250, max_depth=5, ...)
model.fit(X_train_final, y_train)
```
**Gradient Boosting** algorithm use kiya — yeh ek advanced decision tree method hai jo baar baar improve karta rehta hai.

**Step 8 — Accuracy Check:**
```python
r2  = r2_score(y_actual, y_pred)
mae = mean_absolute_error(y_actual, y_pred)
```
- **R² Score** = 1.0 ke paas = perfect (hamare model ka ~0.73)
- **MAE** = Average error in rupees (~38 Lakhs)

**Step 9 — Save:**
```python
pickle.dump(save_data, f)   # model.pkl
json.dump(meta, f)           # meta.json
```
Model + scaler + encoder pickle mein save. Meta JSON mein localities, accuracy info.

